[?2004lTHREAT INTELLIGENCE ADVISORY — Struts Exfil campaign
====================================================

Distribution: TLP:AMBER   Analyst handoff   Confidence: HIGH   (IOCs are defanged)
Affected host: struts-prod-01   Suspected origin IP: 198.51.100.167

1. EXECUTIVE SUMMARY
An external actor executed a multi-stage post-compromise sequence. Endpoint alerting covered only part of it; several persistence and anti-forensic actions were silent. Map every on-disk finding to the ATT&CK techniques below and flag which are NOT in the SAS alert feed.

2. ATT&CK TECHNIQUE MAPPING (MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise)
   T1190      Exploit Public-Facing Application          [initial-access]  step 1: Struts2 OGNL RCE (CVE-2023-50164)
   T1505.003  Web Shell                                  [persistence]  step 2: JSP webshell planted
   T1059.004  Unix Shell                                 [execution]  step 3: shell execution
   T1560.001  Archive via Utility                        [collection]  step 4: stage archive for exfil
   T1048      Exfiltration Over Alternative Protocol     [exfiltration]  step 5: exfiltrate over HTTPS
   T1098.004  SSH Authorized Keys                        [persistence]  step 6: authorized_keys backdoor
   T1053.003  Cron                                       [execution]  step 7: cron persistence
   T1070.002  Clear Linux or Mac System Logs             [defense-evasion]  step 8: selective auth-log wipe

3. RELEVANT VULNERABILITIES (source: NVD, US-Gov public domain)
   CVE-2023-50164  CVSS 9.8 (CRITICAL) v3.1  CWE=CWE-552
      An attacker can manipulate file upload params to enable paths traversal and under some circumstances this can lead to uploading a malicious file which can be used to perform Remote Code Execution.
Users are recommended to upgrade to version
      ref: http://packetstormsecurity.com/files/176157/Struts-S2-066-File-Upload-Remote-Code-Execution.html

4. INDICATORS OF COMPROMISE (defanged)
   ip     198.51.100.167
   c2     update-struts[.]example[.]cn
   pool   stratum+tcp[:]//xmr[.]struts[.]evil[:]3333
   wallet 4A000000000000000000e40b218944d0

Attribution: MITRE ATT&CK(R) (C) The MITRE Corporation, CC BY 4.0. CVE/CVSS from the U.S. National Vulnerability Database (public domain).
