[?2004lique**: T1048 (Exfiltration Over Alterna[?2004h> # Post-Compromise Intrusion Investigation Report
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Executive Summary
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004lo[?2004h> An external threat actor operating from source IP `198.51.100.167` compromised `struts-prod-01` through a multi-stage intrusion. Initial brute-force SSH attempts occurred on 2026-08-08 between 00:54:37 UTC and 00:56:00 UTC (`/disk/var/log/secure:182`), followed by web applications reconnaissance (`/disk/var/log/nginx/access.log:391`). The attacker successfully exploited CVE-2023-50164, an OGNL injection vulnerability in Apache Struts2 (`/disk/opt/tomcat/lib/struts2-core.jar:1`, `/sas/alerts.json:27`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:13`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004lo[?2004h> Following exploitation, the attacker dropped a JSP webshell (`/disk/opt/tomcat/webapps/ROOT/static/upload.jsp:1`), staged a database archive (`/disk/tmp/.cache/dump.tar.gz:1`), exfiltrated sensitive data via HTTPS/HTTP POST to `198.51.100.167` (`/disk/var/log/tomcat/access-exfil.log:116`), established persistent backdoors via SSH authorized_keys (`/disk/root/.ssh/authorized_keys:1`) and cron (`/disk/var/spool/cron/tomcat:5`), and attempted selective log wiping (`/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Threat Entity Profile & Identifiers
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Attacker Source IP**: `198.51.100.167` (`/disk/var/log/secure:213`, `/disk/var/log/nginx/access.log:391`, `/disk/var/log/tomcat/access-exfil.log:116`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:7`)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Command & Control Domain**: `update-struts.example.cn` (`/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:19`)
[?2004l.003 | JSP We[?2004h> - **Mining Pool & Wallet (from persistent payload description)**:
[?2004l[?2004h>   - Pool: `stratum+tcp://xmr.struts.evil:3333` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:20`)
[?2004l[?2004h>   - Wallet: `4A000000000000000000e40b218944d0` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:21`)
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Full Attack Chain & MITRE Enterprise ATT&CK Mapping
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### Step 1: Reconnaissance & Initial Access (T1190 - Exploit Public-Facing Application)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Description**: The threat actor conducted SSH password brute-forcing (`/disk/var/log/secure:182`) gaining access (`/disk/var/log/secure:213`) and probed public endpoints (`/disk/var/log/nginx/access.log:391`). The main web vector was Struts2 OGNL injection (CVE-2023-50164) targeting `/opt/tomcat/lib/struts2-core.jar` (`/disk/opt/tomcat/lib/struts2-core.jar:1`, `/sas/alerts.json:27`, `/sas/vulns.json:44`).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **ATT&CK Technique**: T1190 (Exploit Public-Facing Application) (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:9`)
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### Step 2: Persistence via Web Shell (T1505.003 - Web Shell)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Description**: Upon gaining execution, the attacker dropped a JSP webshell at `/opt/tomcat/webapps/ROOT/static/upload.jsp` (`/disk/opt/tomcat/webapps/ROOT/static/upload.jsp:1`, `/sas/alerts.json:1`).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **ATT&CK Technique**: T1505.003 (Web Shell) (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:10`)
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### Step 3: Command & Shell Execution (T1059.004 - Unix Shell)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Description**: Arbitrary shell commands were executed via the webshell and local shell environments to inspect system resources and prepare staging scripts (`/disk/opt/tomcat/webapps/ROOT/static/upload.jsp:1`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:11`).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **ATT&CK Technique**: T1059.004 (Unix Shell) (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:11`)
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### Step 4: Data Collection & Staging (T1560.001 - Archive via Utility)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Description**: Sensitive database content was dumped and staged as a tar archive disguised as `/tmp/.cache/dump.tar.gz` (`/disk/tmp/.cache/dump.tar.gz:1`, `/sas/alerts.json:10`).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Note**: A separate file `/tmp/.cache/backup.tar.gz` (`/disk/tmp/.cache/backup.tar.gz:1`) was investigated and determined to be a benign scheduled maintenance job (`/disk/tmp/.cache/backup.tar.gz:1`).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **ATT&CK Technique**: T1560.001 (Archive via Utility) (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:12`)
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### Step 5: Data Exfiltration (T1048 - Exfiltration Over Alternative Protocol)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Description**: Staged exfiltration data was transferred out of the network via HTTP/HTTPS POST requests to endpoint `198.51.100.167` (`/disk/var/log/tomcat/access-exfil.log:116`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:13`).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Alert Status**: Silent at endpoint exfiltration destination; captured in web server traffic log (`/disk/var/log/tomcat/access-exfil.log:116`).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **ATT&CK Technique**: T1048 (Exfiltration Over Alternative Protocol) (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:13`)
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### Step 6: SSH Key Backdoor (T1098.004 - SSH Authorized Keys)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Description**: The attacker inserted an unauthorized SSH public key into `/root/.ssh/authorized_keys` (`/disk/root/.ssh/authorized_keys:1`).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Alert Status**: SILENT (Not present in SAS alert feed `/sas/alerts.json:1`).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **ATT&CK Technique**: T1098.004 (SSH Authorized Keys) (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:14`)
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### Step 7: Scheduled Job Persistence (T1053.003 - Cron)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Description**: A malicious cron job was planted under the `tomcat` user cron spool at `/var/spool/cron/tomcat` (`/disk/var/spool/cron/tomcat:5`, `/sas/alerts.json:17`). The job periodic beacon fetches payloads from `http://198.51.100.167/x`.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **ATT&CK Technique**: T1053.003 (Cron) (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:15`)
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### Step 8: Defense Evasion & Anti-Forensics (T1070.002 - Clear Linux or Mac System Logs)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Description**: The attacker executed selective log wiping routines targeting system authentication logs (`/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1`).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Alert Status**: SILENT (Not present in SAS alert feed `/sas/alerts.json:1`).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **ATT&CK Technique**: T1070.002 (Clear Linux or Mac System Logs) (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:16`)
[?2004l[?2004h> 
