[?2004l[?2004hroot@e62f4246bce8:/app# cat << 'EOF' > /app/baseline-report.md
[?2004l[?2004h> # Baseline and Configuration Weakness Report
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Executive Summary
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> A review of system configurations and baseline audit logs for `struts-prod-01` identified multiple critical security weaknesses. These baseline deficiencies enabled initial password brute-forcing, allowed web application exploitation, and permitted post-exploitation persistence and anti-forensics.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Baseline Audit Findings & Weaknesses
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### 1. Outdated and Vulnerable Software Components
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Finding**: Presence of vulnerable Struts2 library `/opt/tomcat/lib/struts2-core.jar` (`/disk/opt/tomcat/lib/struts2-core.jar:1`, `/sas/baseline.json:36`, `/sas/alerts.json:27`).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Impact**: Allowed remote unauthenticated attacker to execute arbitrary code via OGNL injection (CVE-2023-50164) (`/sas/vulns.json:44`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:23`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### 2. Excessive Web Server Write Permissions & Static Directory Execution
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Finding**: Tomcat web application directory `/opt/tomcat/webapps/ROOT/static/` allowed web server process write execution (`/disk/opt/tomcat/webapps/ROOT/static/upload.jsp:1`, `/sas/alerts.json:1`).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Impact**: Allowed attacker to drop and execute JSP webshells directly within web-accessible static directory.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### 3. Weak SSH Authentication & Direct Root SSH Login Enabled
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Finding**: SSH daemon configuration allowed password authentication and direct `root` login, facilitating SSH brute-force password spraying (`/disk/var/log/secure:182`).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Impact**: Attacker successfully brute-forced root SSH password (`/disk/var/log/secure:213`) and subsequently appended persistent keys to `/root/.ssh/authorized_keys` (`/disk/root/.ssh/authorized_keys:1`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### 4. Unmonitored Cron Job Permissions and Spool Security
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Finding**: Lack of strict access control and auditing on user cron spools (`/var/spool/cron/tomcat`) (`/disk/var/spool/cron/tomcat:1`, `/sas/alerts.json:17`).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Impact**: Allowed unprivileged web service accounts to create background persistent tasks beaconing to malicious external IPs (`/disk/var/spool/cron/tomcat:5`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### 5. Inadequate Audit Logging and Log Protection
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Finding**: Local logs were susceptible to unauthorized tampering and deletion without offsite syslog/SIEM forwarding (`/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1`).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Impact**: Threat actor selectively wiped authentication logs to hinder forensic investigation (`/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Baseline Findings Matrix
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> | Baseline Check ID | Weakness Description | Location / Path | Status | Citation |
[?2004l[?2004h> |---|---|---|---|---|
