[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Prioritized Remediation Steps
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### Phase 1: Containment & Isolation (Immediate)
[?2004l[?2004h> 1. **Firewall Blocking**:
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Action: Block inbound traffic from IP `198.51.100.167` (`/disk/var/log/secure:213`, `/disk/var/log/nginx/access.log:391`).
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Verification: Confirm firewall drop rules for `198.51.100.167`.
[?2004l[?2004h> 2. **Quarantine Web Shell**:
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Action: Move `/opt/tomcat/webapps/ROOT/static/upload.jsp` (`/disk/opt/tomcat/webapps/ROOT/static/upload.jsp:1`) to a secure quarantine location (`/var/quarantine/upload.jsp.bak`). Do not outright delete to preserve evidence.
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Verification: Verify `/opt/tomcat/webapps/ROOT/static/upload.jsp` is no longer in the web root.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### Phase 2: Persistence Removal & Account Securing (High Priority)
[?2004l[?2004h> 1. **Remove Backdoor SSH Keys**:
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Action: Backup and clean `/root/.ssh/authorized_keys` (`/disk/root/.ssh/authorized_keys:1`), removing the attacker's public key.
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Verification: Confirm `/root/.ssh/authorized_keys` contains only approved administrative keys.
[?2004l[?2004h> 2. **Remove Malicious Cron Job**:
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Action: Backup `/var/spool/cron/tomcat` (`/disk/var/spool/cron/tomcat:5`) and remove line 5 containing the curl beacon (`http://198.51.100.167/x`).
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Verification: Run `crontab -u tomcat -l` and ensure no unauthorized jobs remain.
[?2004l[?2004h> 3. **Quarantine Staged Exfiltration File**:
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Action: Move `/tmp/.cache/dump.tar.gz` (`/disk/tmp/.cache/dump.tar.gz:1`) to secure forensic storage (`/var/quarantine/dump.tar.gz.bak`). Note that `/tmp/.cache/backup.tar.gz` (`/disk/tmp/.cache/backup.tar.gz:1`) is a legitimate ops maintenance job and must NOT be removed.
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Verification: Check `/tmp/.cache/` directory.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### Phase 3: Vulnerability Remediation & Hardening (Medium Priority)
[?2004l[?2004h> 1. **Upgrade Apache Struts2**:
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Action: Upgrade `/opt/tomcat/lib/struts2-core.jar` (`/disk/opt/tomcat/lib/struts2-core.jar:1`) to a patched version per vendor advisory (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:23`).
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Verification: Verify Struts2 library version and perform regression testing on web application.
[?2004l[?2004h> 2. **SSH Configuration Hardening**:
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Action: Disable SSH password authentication and direct `root` login in `/etc/ssh/sshd_config` (`/disk/var/log/secure:182`).
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Verification: Test SSH access using public key authentication only.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### Phase 4: Recovery & Monitoring (Ongoing)
[?2004l[?2004h> 1. **Centralized Log Forwarding**:
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Action: Configure rsyslog/syslog-ng to forward audit and authentication logs offsite to prevent unmonitored log wiping (`/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1`).
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Verification: Confirm log ingestion on SIEM / central syslog server.
